WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.600
Roman Pearce is an essential part of the "Fast&nbsp;
&amp; Furious" family, and has undergone perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.960
the biggest character change in the franchise.&nbsp;
This is his story, from his teen years growing up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.920
alongside Brian O'Conner to his role as one of the&nbsp;
most integral members of Dominic Toretto's crew.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.000
Not much is known about Roman's youth, but it can&nbsp;
be inferred that a life of crime was pretty much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.520
always in the cards for him. Born and raised&nbsp;
alongside Brian O'Conner in Barstow, California,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.520
Roman and Brian were predisposed to&nbsp;
getting into trouble. In high school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:36.880
their only wholesome activity seemed to be sports.&nbsp;
However, it wasn't long before all that dried up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.440
and the duo found their way on the mean&nbsp;
streets by being particularly good with cars.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.800
However, somewhere along the line, the dynamic duo&nbsp;
separated. While Brian decided to pursue a life in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.080
law enforcement, Roman took the opposite path and&nbsp;
got involved in a local car stealing operation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.960
One day, police raided his garage to find&nbsp;
he was keeping stolen cars inside. He always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.600
wondered if Brian ratted him out, and spent&nbsp;
years behind bars and then under house arrest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:06.560
asking himself that same question, over&nbsp;
and over again. In the course of stewing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.400
on whether his childhood friend betrayed&nbsp;
him, he lost his trust in other people.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.760
When the audience is introduced to Roman in "2&nbsp;
Fast 2 Furious," he's a very angry young man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.360
who has a massive problem with&nbsp;
authority, particularly the police,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:22.240
and has no interest in&nbsp;
reconnecting with Brian O'Conner.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.680
After the events of "The Fast and the Furious,"&nbsp;
Brian O'Conner ends up on the run from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.480
law. He makes his way to Miami where he gets&nbsp;
involved in the local street racing community,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:37.040
but is eventually picked up by the FBI.&nbsp;
Fortunately, his skills make him more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.000
useful in the field than behind bars, and&nbsp;
he is offered the job of posing undercover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.640
as a driver for notorious drug kingpin&nbsp;
Carter Verone — but he needs a partner.

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.360
It's unclear if his past with Roman weighs on&nbsp;
his conscience, or if he just knows Roman is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.800
the right man for the job. Regardless, Brian&nbsp;
insists that his old buddy is the only one who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.760
can assist him in his mission. He travels back&nbsp;
to Barstow to find his friend under house arrest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:05.360
competing in a demolition derby.&nbsp;
After three years behind bars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:09.200
Roman now lives in a trailer and&nbsp;
supports himself with his derby winnings.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.640
Brian offers him a chance to get off&nbsp;
house arrest and have his criminal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.960
record wiped clean by assisting the&nbsp;
FBI. Roman ignores the deal at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:20.723
but becomes enraged when Brian has&nbsp;
the gall to call him by his nickname.

00:02:20.723 --> 00:02:21.723
"Rome!"

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.160
"Only my homeboys call me Rome."

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.800
The two fight, and Brian is&nbsp;
able to best his old friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:38.080
who reluctantly agrees to take the deal. It isn't&nbsp;
the last fight that Roman loses in the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:41.760
and it certainly isn't the last thing&nbsp;
he reluctantly agrees to do for Brian.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.360
Although Roman is no stranger to the type of&nbsp;
driving that this undercover mission requires,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.800
he's definitely in over his head&nbsp;
when it comes to the police work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.880
In his dealings with Verone, he's&nbsp;
combative and even demands more money,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.040
in a move that could absolutely sour the&nbsp;
deal they've worked so hard to achieve.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:04.320
Still, he manages to get hired alongside Brian&nbsp;
for a job running cash for the criminal. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:09.200
they both quickly realize things aren't what&nbsp;
they seem. After discovering FBI trackers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.920
in their cars and learning that officers are&nbsp;
aware that Verone plans to kill his drivers as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.080
soon as the job is done, they realize they&nbsp;
have to take matters into their own hands.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:23.520
The two boys from Barstow hatch a plan to get&nbsp;
everyone in the Miami racing community to conduct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:28.960
a big "scramble" of cars. Their intent is to cover&nbsp;
their exit once the police start pursuing them and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:34.000
the money. Their plan works, but it turns out&nbsp;
that Verone gave them a dummy drop-off location.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:39.040
Roman escapes clean, but he knows that Brian is&nbsp;
caught in the hands of a madman with no backup.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:44.240
This is when he makes the decision that changes&nbsp;
his life forever: Roman goes back for his friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:48.160
despite all the hard feelings he has about&nbsp;
getting arrested, all those years ago.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.840
Family never leaves a brother behind.&nbsp;
Roman crashes his car into Brian's,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:58.000
saving him from getting executed. The&nbsp;
two then pursue Verone onto his yacht&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.080
by jumping their car directly onto&nbsp;
it, causing Roman to break his arm.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:06.320
Fortunately, they're able to take down Verone&nbsp;
and make good on their deal with the FBI.

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.160
With their criminal records expunged,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:11.360
Roman reveals that he hid some&nbsp;
of Verone's money on his person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:16.320
rather than turning it in for evidence. With that,&nbsp;
the reunited friends ride off into the sunset.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:21.520
While the arc of "2 Fast 2 Furious" may look&nbsp;
like a simple story of two friends reconciling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:25.520
their relationship ends up meaning more&nbsp;
in the context of the larger franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:30.240
Brian reveals in the film that his decision to&nbsp;
let Dom go rather than arrest him at the end of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:35.440
"The Fast and the Furious" was motivated out of&nbsp;
guilt over what happened to Roman years earlier.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.120
Therefore, one could argue that the&nbsp;
origin of the Fast family is rooted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.360
in Roman and Brian's friendship, rather&nbsp;
than Brian and Dom's. If Roman and Brian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:47.360
hadn't had such a long history together,&nbsp;
the group may well never have formed.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:53.440
Roman doesn't return to the Fast franchise again&nbsp;
until Brian and Dom are back together as criminal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:58.880
partners on the wrong side of a wanted poster&nbsp;
in "Fast Five." When a Brazilian crime lord pins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:04.640
the murder of a DEA agent on them, they decide to&nbsp;
rob him of $100 million. However, they need help.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:08.160
Among the crack team members they&nbsp;
bring in for the job is Roman Pearce,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:13.040
the resident "talker." But Roman brings a lot&nbsp;
more to the table than just his gift of gab.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.160
He's proven he can fight, drive, and is up for&nbsp;
the crazy stunts the group decides to pull off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:21.120
even if he is often the most reluctant to do so.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:25.120
"This just went from Mission Impossible&nbsp;
to Mission in-freaking-sanity."

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:30.080
That reluctance actually serves as an asset to the&nbsp;
group, when Roman questions the real reason for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:35.120
the score. Roman is unafraid to stand up to Dom,&nbsp;
and suggests that while the money is definitely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:39.760
tempting, it feels like Dom's motivation is&nbsp;
personal. This forces Dom to get real with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:44.240
the people he brought in, and to be completely&nbsp;
open and transparent with them going forward.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:50.000
It's also on this job that Roman's friendship with&nbsp;
fellow Miami car enthusiast Tej becomes apparent.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:55.840
Roman has everything he needs after the team's&nbsp;
success in Brazil. He's fabulously rich,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.840 --> 00:06:00.240
owns a private jet, and even has access&nbsp;
to rare and expensive cars. Moreover,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:04.320
by this point, he's a full-fledged member of the&nbsp;
family. So, even though he doesn't know Letty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:08.720
when Dom asks for his help, he travels to&nbsp;
London to help rescue her. It helps that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:12.720
Brian has worked out a deal for everyone to&nbsp;
get full pardons in exchange for stopping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:17.520
the criminal enterprise that Letty is working&nbsp;
with. For Roman, this means fighting a tank.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:22.720
The group eventually realizes that the leader of&nbsp;
Letty's new gang, Owen Shaw, is trying to attack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:27.120
a heavily armored convoy. Roman is out in&nbsp;
front of everyone when a tank is revealed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.560
Although he's typically considered the&nbsp;
reluctant and cowardly one in the group,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:36.240
Roman steps up in a major way. In fact, he nearly&nbsp;
sacrifices his life by getting out in front of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:41.840
tank and drawing its fire. He manages to dodge the&nbsp;
blast, although his car is severely damaged. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:46.880
makes a daring escape by linking the dead-weight&nbsp;
car to the tank and knocking it off a bridge.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.280
In almost single-handedly taking out the tank,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:53.040
Roman graduates to a whole new level&nbsp;
of criminality and world-saving.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:58.400
After narrowly avoiding being sucked into&nbsp;
a jet engine while taking down Owen Shaw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:03.280
Roman and the rest of Dom's family are finally&nbsp;
allowed to return to Los Angeles after helping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:08.240
apprehend the terrorist. Life is grand ...&nbsp;
until Owen Shaw's brother, Deckard, blows it up.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.640
That's when Roman and the others are recruited&nbsp;
by Mr. Nobody to help him find a piece of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:17.680
revolutionary tracking technology, in exchange&nbsp;
for revenge on Deckard. Always the skeptic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:22.160
Roman says that he's tired of taking orders&nbsp;
and insists on revamping the government's plan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:26.560
However, the plan gets away from him, and Roman&nbsp;
chickens out when tasked with parachuting out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:30.960
of an airplane to attack an armored convoy.&nbsp;
But Tej takes matters into his own hands and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:35.760
manually ejects him. Although he drifts off&nbsp;
course, causing him to show up a little late,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.440
Roman arrives just in the nick of&nbsp;
time to help their plan succeed.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:43.440
Roman proves invaluable to the crew&nbsp;
yet again in Abu Dhabi, when Brian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.240
Dominic, and Letty desperately need a distraction.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:49.840
"Shine brightly, like only Roman Pearce can do.”

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:51.600
“HaHAA!”

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:55.680
With that, Roman picks up the microphone&nbsp;
and successfully distracts the crowd with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.680 --> 00:08:00.560
an impromptu speech, before being accosted&nbsp;
by security. Fortunately, by that time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:04.480
he's caused enough of a distraction for the&nbsp;
rest of the team to pull off their mission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:08.800
and he and Letty are able to escape&nbsp;
in the ensuing ruckus. Afterwards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.040
he rejoins the team as they head back to Los&nbsp;
Angeles. There, his knowledge of the streets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:17.280
he grew up on proves useful in outfoxing&nbsp;
the terrorists using the tracking system.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:23.120
At this point, Roman and the rest of the gang are&nbsp;
a well-oiled, world-saving crime machine. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:27.600
why he doesn't think twice about accepting a call&nbsp;
from Dominic to get the band back together to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:32.960
steal an EMP in Berlin in "Fate of the Furious."&nbsp;
However, he is blindsided by Dominic betraying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:38.240
them and running off to deliver the EMP to a new&nbsp;
enemy named Cipher. Like the rest of the crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.800
Roman is completely shocked by Dom's seemingly&nbsp;
shifting allegiances. On top of that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:47.440
he feels insulted when he learns he just missed&nbsp;
the Top 10 of Interpol's Most Wanted list.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:50.480
"Top 10? That's all right."

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:51.840
"Well, not you, Roman."

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:53.280
"What do you mean?"

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.120
"You just missed the cut. You're number 11."

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.240
Still, despite Roman's personal&nbsp;
feelings of disrespect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:02.480
he's all in for the mission. He suggests&nbsp;
bringing in Brian, but he's reminded that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:06.880
the group agreed at the end of "Furious 7"&nbsp;
to leave him out of their dangerous lifestyle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:11.520
from then on. Roman reluctantly agrees to&nbsp;
let Mr. Nobody and Letty call the shots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:16.400
as they chase Dominic to New York City, only&nbsp;
for his vehicle to be incapacitated by Dom.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:21.520
Even on the heels of yet another betrayal, Roman&nbsp;
refuses to give up on family. He accompanies the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:25.920
rest of the team to Russia to rescue Dominic&nbsp;
from Cipher. Admittedly, the deal has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:30.800
sweetened a bit by the sleek Lamborghini that&nbsp;
he's given to drive. In what are by far the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:35.920
daring conditions Roman has handled a vehicle in&nbsp;
yet, he takes the bright orange sports car out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:40.800
onto the ice as he attempts to outrun a moving&nbsp;
submarine. Unfortunately, it doesn't work out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:45.600
and he loses yet another car. But he is able to&nbsp;
take down a decent number of enemies before he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:50.160
rescued by Tej, and they're able to successfully&nbsp;
save Dom and the rest of the world once again.

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:54.160
Just when it seems like there's&nbsp;
nowhere else for Roman to go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:59.840
an old enemy from Dominc's past returns and&nbsp;
forces the gang to new heights — literally. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:06.240
the trailers for 2021's "F9," we see Roman and Tej&nbsp;
get even more experimental than they already have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:10.560
by taking a car that has been attached to&nbsp;
a rocket engine up into the atmosphere.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.920
"Please tell me that's not a Pontiac&nbsp;
Fiero strapped to a rocket engine?"

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:17.840
"Ahhh, I don't want to die!"

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:22.960
One wonders, as the movies continue,&nbsp;
how much further Roman's story might go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:27.280
as the sky is clearly not the limit. Could&nbsp;
the troubled young kid who was once busted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:32.080
for stealing cars be headed on a world-saving&nbsp;
mission to outer space? Only time will tell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:37.040
but if the past proves anything, it's that&nbsp;
we should never underestimate Roman Pearce.

